    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10371" root="خرطم" body-key="x">[
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَرْطَمٌ</span></b>  (assumed tropical:)  <i>Elongated like a snout</i> or <i>nose;</i> and
so, app., ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخْرَنْطِمٌ</span></b> : see a verse cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتَاوِجُ</span>.
Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِفَافٌ مُخَرْطَمَةٌ</span> [in the sing. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُفٌّ مُخَرْطَمٌ</span>
(occurring in the K in art <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فقع</span>)] <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَاتُ</span>
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَرَاطِيمَ</span></b> ; i. e. (assumed tropical:)  [<i>Boots</i>] <i>having their fore parts
pointed.</i> (TA.)

